Notebook[{
Cell["Part 4. Composite systems: tensor product and partial trace", "Section",
 CellID->874461601,ExpressionUUID->"22a1a762-10e3-861e-525e-3f4ca097ed64"],

Cell["\<\
Two quantum systems join by the tensor product, and the reverse question, \
what one subsystem looks like once the other is ignored, is answered by the \
partial trace. This Part builds each direction from primitives and then \
confirms that the framework object agrees: the tensor product is a Kronecker \
product, and the partial trace is a reshape-and-contract.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->36768919,ExpressionUUID->"4da796ef-9f57-a4bf-7b5c-0fc91ae30e85"],

Cell["\<\
4.1 [BSc] How do I form the tensor product of states and of operators?\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1699946459,ExpressionUUID->"1b39f900-6440-cee7-4ac6-f16a0dfa94cd"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Two subsystems combine by the tensor product: states as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "75d93363-5da6-51a4-23e6-ab4d5453238e"],
 ", operators as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["B", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a568a6-87a2-527f-535a-810032572145"],
 ", and the two are compatible, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["(",
      SpanMaxSize->1], 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      StyleBox["B", "TI"]}], 
     StyleBox[")",
      SpanMaxSize->1]}], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}]}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["A", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}], "\[CircleTimes]", 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["B", "TI"], 
      TemplateBox[{
        StyleBox["\[Phi]", "TI"]},
       "Ket"]}], ")"}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "00d7f70d-8d0e-ae34-30ec-ef5724b8f51e"],
 ". The joint system carries one amplitude for every pair of subsystem \
labels, so the composite lives in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "1"], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2f3e8453-9762-68ea-56c5-1e1d22173a30"],
 "-dimensional product space, and in the computational basis the tensor \
product is exactly the Kronecker product."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1535504786,ExpressionUUID->"5902d484-617f-9570-0f31-cdee100bfc5a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["WL",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : the tensor product of two single-qubit amplitude vectors ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "56e0e12c-de7d-6135-7e9f-f889db08301f"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5708d032-2150-04f2-7d37-ca7c50e56ed8"],
 ", flattened into one length-4 vector, one amplitude per computational label \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"00", ",", "01", ",", "10", ",", "11"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7807e8-9504-b25a-6907-9eb21cb600a0"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1208482393,ExpressionUUID->"166f8969-5e31-e8e5-3e14-21335bc5bacf"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
  RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[1]:= ",
 CellID->28909615,ExpressionUUID->"234f1fb7-07c6-bba9-5174-96f1b27009f3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Operators combine the same way; here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6ee45b93-a0df-d1f6-169c-52dcd16ba3dc"],
 " as the Kronecker product of the two matrices."
}], "Text",
 CellID->193832008,ExpressionUUID->"0a3edd72-e0d3-62fb-3bc5-d53f916630c1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[2]:= ",
 CellID->684317082,ExpressionUUID->"6ec9a758-58be-624c-16f6-3f02594b3096"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The compatibility rule is what makes this a tensor product: acting with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "23253b8d-1c99-a6bf-52da-b2d7952d0c85"],
 " on the product state is the same as acting with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["X", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e84829b-9667-6594-16bb-1bc523124ffe"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Z", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "569e173f-6b36-b240-7ea5-8f790ec000aa"],
 " on the two factors separately, for every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["a", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["b", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["c", "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox["d", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a3e88e-0b57-fa6e-4350-01e8aee3c8b4"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->528485616,ExpressionUUID->"779c57de-bb93-d239-1da4-4e983e27a103"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "==", " ", 
  
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}]}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}], " ", ".", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[3]:= ",
 CellID->1392207227,ExpressionUUID->"2867ea9b-6e8d-517b-581c-03c50b382041"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["QF",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumTensorProduct"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "76dfbc62-92ac-7b6e-1ee4-364c275949b4"],
 " performs the same join but keeps the factor structure. The result is a \
two-qubit ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumState"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0df4b6a5-173c-e15a-3b8b-2f0fa2ceb3a0"],
 ", shown as its summary box."
}], "Text",
 CellID->705466992,ExpressionUUID->"4d620fc7-5cf2-d9d8-7b11-a6a15484ab22"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"tp", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[4]:= ",
 CellID->1350516518,ExpressionUUID->"741b091d-feb2-1a39-1c38-a146fb476903"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<StateVector\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3bf5a20e-c541-e06e-698a-446becf5b2b4"],
 " reads the amplitudes back out."
}], "Text",
 CellID->907546795,ExpressionUUID->"07964fa7-8d1e-ff14-2dae-660124a8c27e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"tp", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], " ", "//", " ", 
  "Normal"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[5]:= ",
 CellID->814772321,ExpressionUUID->"3e367b18-9aa8-58f9-67ce-73421f5d2ac3"],

Cell["The object route and the hand computation agree.", "Text",
 CellID->1054628905,ExpressionUUID->"1dbaaaf7-1388-e538-4b59-43b1a622cc02"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"tp", "[", "\"\<StateVector\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[6]:= ",
 CellID->2043779557,ExpressionUUID->"77d99fdb-a351-2d53-1de6-1684d6e477b9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "It joins operators the same way; here ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "04646437-faee-7dfc-2c1c-7e70fe9b47c6"],
 " kept as a ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumOperator"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1cbde497-e826-5557-4442-fdd089d33fbd"],
 ", shown as its summary box."
}], "Text",
 CellID->17830494,ExpressionUUID->"6ecb37d0-fbcc-3e82-16c8-ae9dfe7e84e8"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"xz", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[7]:= ",
 CellID->1589986527,ExpressionUUID->"4c358d3e-86d3-ec5f-75ca-25783367b6a5"],

Cell["Its matrix is the Kronecker product built by hand.", "Text",
 CellID->943101875,ExpressionUUID->"1f908cf3-3c70-d55a-45af-25bdb50abfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
   RowBox[{"xz", "[", "\"\<Matrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "1", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"PauliMatrix", "[", "3", "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[8]:= ",
 CellID->67888809,ExpressionUUID->"5dac66ba-272d-3627-0b54-7fe452d99d0d"],

Cell["\<\
The compatibility rule holds at the object level too: the joint operator \
applied to the joint state is the tensor product of the two factor images, \
equal as states.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1432876021,ExpressionUUID->"110914de-bbdd-83a1-4736-8d983e69d18b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"xz", "[", "tp", "]"}], " ", "==", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumTensorProduct", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<X\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"a", ",", " ", "b"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"QuantumOperator", "[", "\"\<Z\>\"", "]"}], "[", 
     RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"c", ",", " ", "d"}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[9]:= ",
 CellID->876231958,ExpressionUUID->"76d004f9-29e5-6665-1eef-9da34f904d4f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both give the amplitude vector ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    StyleBox["a", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["c", "TI"]}], ",", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"a", "d"}], "TI"], ",", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"b", "c"}], "TI"], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["b", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2c76c797-c249-79ca-540d-ded0f7fc4b10"],
 ", the pairwise products of the two factors' amplitudes, and the operator ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["X", "TI"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   StyleBox["Z", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "35077f55-9291-6519-633d-771f27244c63"],
 ", and both confirm the compatibility rule for arbitrary amplitudes: the \
composite factorizes into its parts, and the framework object additionally \
knows it is a two-qubit system (its factors, order, and basis), a matrix \
being one representation read from it."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1020575516,ExpressionUUID->"4ebf3687-f906-130d-7644-afe0f8b37e57"],

Cell["\<\
4.2 [BSc] How do I take a partial trace of a two-party state and obtain a \
reduced density matrix?\
\>", "Subsection",
 CellID->1967685850,ExpressionUUID->"65de4a87-3471-cd9f-13e6-63e1bd0597e5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The state of subsystem ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bedd9bd-1d84-ddaa-2992-d0e79436a7f0"],
 " alone is the reduced density matrix ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "=", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["Tr",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox[
     RowBox[{"A", "B"}], "TI"]], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4c37f35a-e1a6-07fe-75cc-eb0790536dc4"],
 ", formed by tracing out ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "02f88238-86c8-66df-3287-2462337d4c25"],
 ": an average over everything in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "034d641c-5834-e412-3173-7e4659c6cf78"],
 " that is not observed, keeping only what ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "52ce4f6a-032d-a48b-02f6-6734b6d90ed1"],
 " can still predict on its own. For a product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["A", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5bfe104a-50de-a555-0985-8a1461680fbf"],
 " stays pure; for an ",
 StyleBox["entangled", "TI"],
 " state it comes out mixed, which is the operational signature of \
entanglement. Take the one-parameter family ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"00"},
      "Ket"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"11"},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "134534fb-1061-d656-417a-ada5a115bcbc"],
 ", which runs from the product state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{"00"},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2cd98fd2-34e7-e188-54e6-269cbc93b3d2"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6e1c99a5-dcef-9c28-1623-100ed49be772"],
 " to the Bell state ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    SuperscriptBox["\[CapitalPhi]", "+"]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "608e87cc-8fce-afdf-10b5-1e962a78f525"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2aa912c6-4938-1bb7-5a56-8ba068cd699d"],
 "; every two-qubit pure state is one of these up to local unitaries, its \
Schmidt form (Part 11, 11.3)."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1044562475,ExpressionUUID->"66b4bee0-d247-b105-0e4b-37cde7f3006f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["WL",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : the amplitudes of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    RowBox[{
      StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
      StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
      StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
   "Ket"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "337c2d89-644e-5b5e-6103-c4d30dfb29a4"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1653200050,ExpressionUUID->"5f7c2741-1c81-ec9b-0503-bf2b9535b6e1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], ",", " ", "0", ",", " ", "0", ",",
     " ", 
    RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[10]:= ",
 CellID->1384978530,ExpressionUUID->"644cc522-c7c4-9b18-0c73-dc8ff276e662"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its density matrix is the outer product ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Ket"], 
   TemplateBox[{
     StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"]},
    "Bra"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2de8c8f9-eaf3-8e90-5b97-e1a28e87d4fa"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->519689844,ExpressionUUID->"6801f052-da94-0b6f-183e-ea1fdf2159b5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rho", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
    RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "psi", "]"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[11]:= ",
 CellID->1609367578,ExpressionUUID->"0daf8e98-7628-e40b-3b54-27c203c2cf51"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Reshape the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"4", "\[Times]", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7b6211f5-475c-1194-2911-88bf72e963fe"],
 " matrix into a ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"2", "\[Times]", "2", "\[Times]", "2", "\[Times]", "2"}]], 
  "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c8f7bdf-2493-8d8a-24b5-72994d27d7d0"],
 " tensor, whose four legs are ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["ket",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["ket",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["bra",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]], ",", 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["bra",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], 
    StyleBox["B", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14e8dcaf-74c9-37ba-3c97-d5097d7d9d80"],
 ", and trace out ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5d5cbd3a-e88d-ee42-0b63-35678939b4a8"],
 " by contracting its two legs, indices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"4", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3b7fe4cc-5889-7f4e-6904-fd96593c4594"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6cb5c01f-62f5-68e0-144a-da5916803aca"],
 " is a real angle."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1541450781,ExpressionUUID->"55f417ec-7166-d78d-038b-8eb60010bdd7"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"rhoA", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"TensorContract", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rho", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], 
       "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[12]:= ",
 CellID->1657269721,ExpressionUUID->"4b6e5dad-9702-0c1f-7916-54f722b75765"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["Tr",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["[",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   SubsuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"], "2"], 
   StyleBox["]",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "1d359769-845f-cd94-44ca-0f332deb97fe"],
 " measures how much of the pair's structure the reduction kept."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1140508347,ExpressionUUID->"2055bfee-d4b5-7aa2-506a-36cbdd404888"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"purityA", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
     RowBox[{"rhoA", " ", ".", " ", "rhoA"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[13]:= ",
 CellID->496109794,ExpressionUUID->"64c30c0d-1857-1b13-0cf0-a65799e26679"],

Cell["\<\
At the two ends of the family, the product state and the Bell state.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->108435171,ExpressionUUID->"46632a09-cc5f-b0ef-6e10-cc52e5eb0235"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"purityA", " ", "/.", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", "0"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "->", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Pi", "/", "4"}]}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[14]:= ",
 CellID->829388421,ExpressionUUID->"6ea251ed-865f-e03c-1652-48b733ebb306"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["QF",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : ",
 Cell[BoxData["QuantumPartialTrace"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "25a0bfbe-b1d4-2428-535f-36fbc0668f72"],
 " traces out the listed qubit in one call and returns the reduced state as \
an object, shown as its summary box."
}], "Text",
 CellID->203008389,ExpressionUUID->"04786d0e-016a-d127-2c07-8568b01ca00d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"redA", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "psi", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[15]:= ",
 CellID->1090263105,ExpressionUUID->"2d15b43a-cd49-5244-5b2a-2e67e4fc20ae"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<Purity\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2d1ff276-b82a-c3ca-5b24-f43039dc9110"],
 " is the same function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "14fd1512-f616-8834-3c82-8d5f83a0db1e"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1560876240,ExpressionUUID->"66c67103-72a1-9427-0efe-696d0755ff0d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"redA", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[16]:= ",
 CellID->176337227,ExpressionUUID->"48c794f4-84f6-2bfc-78fc-0dbe2c8379c6"],

Cell["The hand computation and the framework agree.", "Text",
 CellID->807053435,ExpressionUUID->"58ee7ecb-1370-1005-0896-7795a605636f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"redA", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
    " ", "rhoA"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[17]:= ",
 CellID->1633675818,ExpressionUUID->"11d04a92-cbef-a8a5-47e0-63dfed9bfa8f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The two ends of the family are named states: the Bell pair ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<PhiPlus\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7d9821c9-0e61-bc6d-2ba7-b893ab1506b7"],
 " and a product ket such as ",
 Cell[BoxData["\"\<01\>\""], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3181a460-bc62-f1ee-67be-3e4a3514c334"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1828793009,ExpressionUUID->"3937e1d4-04c3-e55a-68cc-f89ead77cfa0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", "#", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], " ", 
   "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"{", 
   RowBox[{"\"\<PhiPlus\>\"", ",", " ", "\"\<01\>\""}], "}"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[18]:= ",
 CellID->1232986364,ExpressionUUID->"6b45e796-37a7-eecc-197a-fed04253b416"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both give ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["\[Rho]", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["A", "TI"]], "=", 
   StyleBox["diag",
    FontSlant->"Plain"], 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["cos",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox[
      StyleBox["sin",
       FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5e187950-8ca2-2ab2-0638-711a25577898"],
 " with purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "250a2d7c-9b81-05b0-5309-c5261e346f9a"],
 ": the reduced state carries the Schmidt weights on its diagonal, pure at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "0"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "15a9104d-5625-6af3-4356-8a1763d038d9"],
 " where the pair is a product and the maximally mixed ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["I", "TI"], "/", "2"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "58c17d8b-1b7e-6f79-08ff-74d59e0b3243"],
 " at ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "=", "\[Pi]", "/", "4"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "43821c38-6720-b4f9-71b1-966212da1ec3"],
 " where the pair is maximally entangled, so the mixedness of the reduced \
state is exactly the entanglement discarded along with ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["B", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "341c54d9-3079-6bba-5c24-4d83410c3980"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->762269937,ExpressionUUID->"1dbf9c2b-d84a-d79b-4b44-1674d9fcbde1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["A heterogeneous register.",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " The reshape-and-contract recipe does not care that the qudits differ in \
size. In the two-qubit case each qubit owned a ket leg and a bra leg; the \
same holds for qudits of any dimensions. Take three qudits of dimensions ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], "2"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], "3"]}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1], "=", 
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "0f449897-1a0e-51e7-357b-11d19fbb23cd"],
 " in the same family, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     RowBox[{
       StyleBox["\[Psi]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox["(", SpanMaxSize -> 1], 
       StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
       StyleBox[")", SpanMaxSize -> 1]}]},
    "Ket"], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"0,0,0"},
      "Ket"]}], "+", 
    RowBox[{
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], 
     StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], 
     TemplateBox[{"1,1,1"},
      "Ket"]}]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6d5a63ab-93b9-14f3-1b7a-7af5264c7ed9"],
 ", living in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "3"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "2"], "\[CircleTimes]", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "5"], "=", 
   SuperscriptBox["\:2102", "30"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5077c06e-c394-b43c-000c-da4bf6261f06"],
 ". The joint density matrix is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"30", "\[Times]", "30"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "07359582-e823-44a1-2eca-0cef89d62e8b"],
 "; reshaped to a rank-6 array of shape ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "2", ",", "5", ",", "3", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7c239bd0-3ff5-3b18-25d0-129ab9818662"],
 ", its first three axes are the ket (row) legs of particles ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"1", ",", "2", ",", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "68c76573-72ce-0c1a-18fd-7d3d077b5760"],
 " and the last three the bra (column) legs, so particle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6184d2f2-049e-728e-17bb-cbbcad2b40d4"],
 " owns ket-leg ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4fd967ef-5008-0b29-75e7-7ec961bd5673"],
 " and bra-leg ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "+", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "19bb1c5e-57ab-6e36-4f58-9618625e351c"],
 ", each of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox[
   StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
   StyleBox["p", "TI"]]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5c8dcc56-7aa9-964a-04b2-e6107f5dfc90"],
 ". Tracing out a set of particles contracts their leg pairs, and the legs \
that survive, grouped into rows and columns, are the reduced density matrix \
on the remaining qudits, of size ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["kept",
     FontSlant->"Plain"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30baa1c8-66ad-75e0-6059-389213585fca"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->405213039,ExpressionUUID->"52535901-cb26-8b9c-0261-516aeed0d9e6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["WL",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : build the two basis kets from the dimension list, one level ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["k", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "323a4b1c-b138-a791-63da-6359c0b20dfb"],
 " on every qudit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->2118931930,ExpressionUUID->"7421cf44-a1ac-4319-1dde-e721d0592e63"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"kets", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Table", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
      RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", " ", "@@", " ", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"UnitVector", "[", 
           RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", "k"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], ")"}]}], 
      "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"k", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[19]:= ",
 CellID->1039057480,ExpressionUUID->"511b3347-8d7d-ab60-0738-ab212409f64a"],

Cell["Combine them with the Schmidt weights.", "Text",
 CellID->1411198270,ExpressionUUID->"36c19c85-764d-0b01-5efe-15ef03f8566b"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"psi", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Cos", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"kets", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "+", " ", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Sin", "[", "\[Lambda]", "]"}], " ", 
     RowBox[{"kets", "[", 
      RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}]}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[20]:= ",
 CellID->1703453532,ExpressionUUID->"6815cd54-0cd7-196f-182a-e51ea5626bb5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Reshape its density matrix to the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "2", ",", "5", ",", "3", ",", "2", ",", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "519775d4-d545-25f2-07ad-6c91dcf18fd8"],
 " tensor."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1477609488,ExpressionUUID->"5900aac7-5263-773e-0f3f-43a167165a04"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rhoT", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"ArrayReshape", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"KroneckerProduct", "[", 
      RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"Conjugate", "[", "psi", "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
      "3", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "5", ",", " ", "3", ",", " ", "2", ",", 
       " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[21]:= ",
 CellID->1030824397,ExpressionUUID->"06ecfdb3-2197-c9b0-2e93-f4fd50239b9a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remove the dimension-",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "12d95fcb-3316-2212-42e7-569546a37178"],
 " qudit (particle ",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "733995c2-f5bf-78ee-22c6-0caffc4a4a34"],
 ") by contracting legs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"5", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "4f8ab258-7e7f-0723-7589-34027b0a6a09"],
 ", then group the surviving ket legs into rows and bra legs into columns."
}], "Text",
 CellID->100031176,ExpressionUUID->"6b12ee74-9953-131d-1921-003e18e67e67"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"rho13", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"Flatten", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"TensorContract", "[", 
      RowBox[{"rhoT", ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}], "}"}]}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", 
        RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "4"}], "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[22]:= ",
 CellID->144223354,ExpressionUUID->"65262d3c-fccc-1dc6-0cdd-c579f579672c"],

Cell["Its size is the product of the kept dimensions.", "Text",
 CellID->1443527617,ExpressionUUID->"5e157ee2-48da-d240-062b-77cc696ca0aa"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Dimensions", "[", "rho13", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[23]:= ",
 CellID->311511756,ExpressionUUID->"78287f93-0f12-7c52-2828-76ddaaa746b8"],

Cell["\<\
It is a state: the input is normalized, and the reduction has unit trace, is \
Hermitian, and has a nonnegative spectrum, the two Schmidt weights and zeros.\
\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1381425643,ExpressionUUID->"08285353-0e0e-39f8-3828-4b1dabb88bc2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"Norm", "[", "psi", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Tr", "[", "rho13", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"HermitianMatrixQ", "[", "rho13", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Eigenvalues", "[", "rho13", "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:= ",
 CellID->377280352,ExpressionUUID->"1daed7d3-93e8-7698-4b55-ce9d259d5ce2"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its purity is the same function of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "187adc3d-3961-76c2-4819-d667b8145c28"],
 " as the qubit pair's."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1717363484,ExpressionUUID->"641c78eb-7f03-7846-0c24-71b57ab64aac"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Tr", "[", 
    RowBox[{"rho13", " ", ".", " ", "rho13"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[25]:= ",
 CellID->1781880651,ExpressionUUID->"5bfcc75d-c21d-6fb0-0983-df06f7a8359a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Remove two qudits at once: particle ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "112ae6ec-4b5c-6ad2-4729-ffb66ee93838"],
 " owns legs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["p", "TI"]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6121b9de-dddd-aca8-10de-309bd469f6f2"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["p", "TI"], "+", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "30209679-023a-ee91-61df-0823b7ccb4fb"],
 ", so each pair of particles contracts two leg pairs, and the pairs ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"2", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "1"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "}"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"{", "2"}], ",", 
   RowBox[{"3", "}"}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "29bc1606-c22d-409d-5f43-8863f7d812e7"],
 " leave the dimension-",
 Cell[BoxData["5"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7bf1e1bf-5b3e-c64b-298e-f8f95ec8ac91"],
 ", dimension-",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "3119d855-3ffd-7401-6726-d21fb9885f6b"],
 ", and dimension-",
 Cell[BoxData["3"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62a6d1b5-4e36-fa69-125d-c8ff6bc0c8b3"],
 " qudit."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1536527082,ExpressionUUID->"7c41cdc9-5ab3-1ef5-247e-e4935f4664df"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"pairs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"TensorContract", "[", 
       RowBox[{"rhoT", ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
         RowBox[{"{", 
          RowBox[{"#", ",", " ", 
           RowBox[{"#", " ", "+", " ", "3"}]}], "}"}], "]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
      "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
       RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[26]:= ",
 CellID->1621535814,ExpressionUUID->"51fce014-dca1-0630-0783-fa51d5546d1a"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["QF",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 " : the framework needs only the amplitudes and the dimension list to build \
the same register."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1193935837,ExpressionUUID->"657c1c65-980e-511d-1303-964f19bb2067"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"qs", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumState", "[", 
   RowBox[{"psi", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"3", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "5"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[27]:= ",
 CellID->105329933,ExpressionUUID->"0f15dbd5-5f35-596c-352a-d29f5ac02bb6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Trace out the dimension-",
 Cell[BoxData["2"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7e9b7e66-629a-1114-26b9-7040172f607e"],
 " qudit once, as an object that keeps the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "585a51e6-774f-2dd2-087a-48c002fa7738"],
 " factorization."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1234416869,ExpressionUUID->"1d7c0b5b-c40c-ea6a-4b03-a304edbeb8b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"red2", " ", "=", " ", 
  RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
   RowBox[{"qs", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[28]:= ",
 CellID->240380995,ExpressionUUID->"370294fd-9e49-2d35-5d31-0da71bfc741f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Its dimensions are reported as ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   StyleBox["(",
    SpanMaxSize->1], 
   RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}], 
   StyleBox[")",
    SpanMaxSize->1]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "2845529c-454d-b13b-587b-4bc66cf90001"],
 " rather than the flattened ",
 Cell[BoxData["15"], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "7519012f-e657-215b-2326-988893e273a1"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellID->1771870337,ExpressionUUID->"594776df-9e75-d16a-0f7d-6f991b01a3b0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"red2", "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[29]:= ",
 CellID->305160771,ExpressionUUID->"6405505f-4b92-3bd6-0c3b-4a196e24893c"],

Cell["Its purity is the hand value.", "Text",
 CellID->1896945989,ExpressionUUID->"6878c7f8-419e-9db5-1807-dea27028e79f"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"red2", "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[30]:= ",
 CellID->653417278,ExpressionUUID->"48a3d607-c312-9dd3-7850-c860f6a4e739"],

Cell["The hand matrix and the framework's agree.", "Text",
 CellID->1067269536,ExpressionUUID->"539491e8-328f-8d7b-01ab-08b2473bd441"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
     RowBox[{"red2", "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", "]"}], "]"}], " ", "==", 
    " ", "rho13"}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[31]:= ",
 CellID->49659130,ExpressionUUID->"7fcf59b5-a5ca-2155-25f5-50fecc7f73bf"],

Cell["The dimensions left by each single removal.", "Text",
 CellID->464508221,ExpressionUUID->"023f49e2-a747-9723-33c5-60cfd2f3fa09"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
     RowBox[{"qs", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Dimensions\>\"", "]"}], 
   " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
  RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"{", "1", "}"}]}], "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[32]:= ",
 CellID->1361313038,ExpressionUUID->"21aa1c49-e16c-f406-57a9-9612901edf6c"],

Cell["The three pair removals equal the hand contractions.", "Text",
 CellID->1907680634,ExpressionUUID->"289b85cd-827f-9a9c-58b8-1c97370be8e6"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"(", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"Normal", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
          RowBox[{"qs", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<DensityMatrix\>\"", 
         "]"}], "]"}], " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"{", "2", "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ")"}], " ", "==", " ", "pairs"}], 
   ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[33]:= ",
 CellID->483148123,ExpressionUUID->"12f3dbee-abc4-6375-4280-d2cbce714e5f"],

Cell["\<\
The purity of all six reductions, the three single removals followed by the \
three pairs.\
\>", "Text",
 CellID->1195452142,ExpressionUUID->"7ed5da6f-a344-b859-26ea-dc48d6f60aa3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Simplify", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"QuantumPartialTrace", "[", 
       RowBox[{"qs", ",", " ", "#"}], "]"}], "[", "\"\<Purity\>\"", "]"}], 
     " ", "&"}], " ", "/@", " ", 
    RowBox[{"Subsets", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"Range", "[", "3", "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"1", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], ",", " ", 
   RowBox[{"\[Lambda]", " ", "\[Element]", " ", "Reals"}]}], "]"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[34]:= ",
 CellID->1521685512,ExpressionUUID->"2cfa2c34-ef50-7d46-5499-c6718ae547ac"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Both routes give reductions of dimension ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   UnderscriptBox["\[Product]", 
    StyleBox["kept",
     FontSlant->"Plain"],
    LimitsPositioning->False], 
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["q", "TI"]]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "362a4e41-4988-041f-5e2a-602b683d6f65"],
 ", ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "5"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "5"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["(",
     SpanMaxSize->1], 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "2"}], 
    StyleBox[")",
     SpanMaxSize->1]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "01ed6b92-5a5f-fa78-3792-82dc5febc942"],
 " for the single removals and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"5", ",", "2", ",", "3"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "107fa29c-d013-1000-4004-3bd9e1a6636a"],
 " for the pairs, and every one of the six carries the same spectrum, the two \
Schmidt weights ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["cos",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}], ",", 
   RowBox[{
    SuperscriptBox[
     StyleBox["sin",
      FontSlant->"Plain"], "2"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
    StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "6798df62-4cc7-e4e1-0da7-d74c6573cecb"],
 " padded with zeros, hence the same purity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["cos",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"], "+", 
   SuperscriptBox[
    StyleBox["sin",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "4"], "\[ThinSpace]", 
   StyleBox["\[Lambda]", "TI"]}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "49f5450b-e8d1-97dd-7f8b-5d548965fd27"],
 ": the state is entangled across every cut with the same Schmidt weights, \
and which qudit sizes sit on either side of the cut does not enter. The \
contraction is the same construction at any sizes; only the leg dimensions \
change, and where the hand computation sees a flattened square matrix, the \
framework keeps the qudit factorization and reports its dimensions \
accordingly."
}], "Text",
 CellID->97201263,ExpressionUUID->"2570a8a5-7a6f-59e7-530f-410f7f1a2bcd"]
},
FrontEndVersion->"15.0 for Mac OS X ARM (64-bit) (February 17, 2026)",
